  "privacy": "Privacy",
  "privacyText": "Your texts stay on your phone and are never uploaded. Voices are produced on the device by your phone's text-to-speech engine. Text in photos is read on the device with Google ML Kit; photos are not sent anywhere, but ML Kit may send Google anonymous diagnostic data (such as device model and error codes). In hands-free mode the microphone is used only on the device, in real time, to notice when you have finished speaking. If you turn on “Check what I say”, your speech is turned into text by your phone's on-device speech recognition; the app never uses online recognition. Nothing is recorded or sent. In \"Recite from memory\" mode your speech is transcribed on the phone by the open-source Whisper model, downloaded once. The only exception is \"Record voices\": lines are recorded only when you tap \"Record\", and the recordings stay on the phone and are never sent.",
